.TH FALSE 1 "2026" "ntlibc" "ntlibc User Commands"
.SH NAME
false \- do nothing, unsuccessfully
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B false
.RI [ operand ] .\|.\|.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B false
exits with a return status that indicates unsuccessful completion. It
can be invoked with any combination of options and operands; all are
ignored.
.PP
Shares its implementation with the
.I sh
built-in of the same name; see
.BR true (1)
for the exact split between
.BR src/util/false.c 's
.B __util_false_main()
and
.BR src/sh/builtin.c 's
.B bi_false() .
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH OPERANDS
None; any operands given are ignored without error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B >0
Always; this implementation always exits 1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR true (1)
